    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0631" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg549"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr. Romero</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,
                            Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 24, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communications of September 21 and October 24 last, with their several
                    accompaniments, all of which have reference to the decree issued on the 2d of
                    May, 1865, by the Congress of the United States of Colombia, in honor of Don
                    Benito Juarez, the president of the republic of Mexico,</p>
                <p>You will be pleased to accept my thanks for the information thus kindly
                    communicated by you to this government, and to receive the assurances of my very
                    distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W, HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Señor <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matias Romero, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
